-- title:
--   Special-fibre pⁿ-torsion in abelian-quotient coordinates at p ∥ M
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a non-zero natural number with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $p$ in the sense that $p$ is a non-unit of $A$, with residue field $\kappa = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ algebraically closed of characteristic $p$. Let $\Lambda$ be a `LevelData` for $(p,M,H,A)$, consisting of a structure morphism $\sigma_A : \operatorname{Spec} A \to \mathrm{base}\,p$ with $\mathrm{barPt}\,A$ followed by $\sigma_A$ equal to $\mathrm{genPt}\,p$, a scheme over $\mathrm{base}\,p$ with a relative group law, and bijections identifying its generic and special sections with $J_H(M/p)$ at the pushed-down level and with $\mathrm{Pic}^0_\kappa(\mathrm{Fbar}\,p\,M\,H\,\kappa)$; let $O$ be a `JHNeronObjectAtP` over $\Lambda$, with structure morphism $O.g$, relative group law $O.L$, generic-point bijection $O.\mathrm{pts} : J_H(M) \simeq \{\text{sections of } O.g \text{ over } \mathrm{genPt}\,p\}$, and special-fibre bijection $O.\mathrm{ptsSp}$ from the glued Picard group $\mathrm{GluedPic0}\,\kappa\,(\mathrm{Fbar}\,p\,M\,H\,\kappa)\,O.\mathrm{ssFinset}$ onto the sections of $O.g$ over $\mathrm{resPt}\,A$ followed by $\sigma_A$. Let $n > 0$. Three assertions hold. First, for every pair $b$ of degree-zero divisor classes of $\mathrm{Fbar}\,p\,M\,H\,\kappa$ over $\kappa$ with $p^n \cdot b = 0$ there are $x \in O.\mathrm{finPts}(p^n)$ — the subgroup of $J_H(M)$ generated by the $p^n$-torsion classes of $\mathrm{Pic}^0_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}(\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}\,M\,H)$ whose associated generic section extends to a section over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ — a section $s$ of $O.g$ over $\sigma_A$ with $(O.\mathrm{pts}\,x)_1 = \mathrm{barPt}\,A$ followed by $s_1$, and a section $s_\kappa$ over $\mathrm{resPt}\,A \ggg \sigma_A$ with $(s_\kappa)_1 = \mathrm{resPt}\,A$ followed by $s_1$, such that $\mathrm{toPic0Pair}\,O.\mathrm{ssFinset}(O.\mathrm{ptsSp}^{-1} s_\kappa) = b$, where $\mathrm{toPic0Pair}$ sends a glued class to the pair of classes of its two divisor components. Secondly, for every $x \in O.\mathrm{finPts}(p^n)$ and all such $s$ and $s_\kappa$, the image $\mathrm{toPic0Pair}\,O.\mathrm{ssFinset}(O.\mathrm{ptsSp}^{-1} s_\kappa)$ vanishes if and only if $O.\mathrm{ptsSp}^{-1} s_\kappa$ itself vanishes. Thirdly, for every $x$ in $O.\mathrm{toricPts}(p^n)$, the subgroup of $J_H(M)$ generated by the image of $O.\mathrm{toricPoint}(p^n)$, and all such $s$ and $s_\kappa$, one has $O.\mathrm{ptsSp}^{-1} s_\kappa = 0$.
--
--   This is the group-theoretic half of the description of the $p^n$-torsion of the identity component of the Néron model of $J_H(M)$ at a prime $p$ exactly dividing $M$: the finite part surjects, in abelian-quotient coordinates, onto the $p^n$-torsion of the product of the two degree-zero Picard groups of the special fibre, with kernel precisely the classes of trivial reduction, and the toric classes reduce to zero. It feeds the construction of Hecke-equivariant finite-part classes used further on in the level-lowering and lifting arguments.
